"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff scheduled for July 15th, 2023. The project involves leveraging AI for data visualization and secure file sharing prototypes. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and prototype testing ahead of schedule. The project budget was adjusted to $550,000 to cover scope realization, including real-time analytics, and a separate $15,000 budget was approved for training. Stakeholders were asked to submit ideas by July 20th and feedback by the end of November. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, were updated to take effect in January. A celebration for the milestone was held on October 10th."
